      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Panels installed on an east-north-east roof with approx. 23 degree slope.  System generates power from sunrise to early afternoon (my household's peak electricity usage time) negating the need for a costly battery.  System generates approx. 10 kws @ winter solace rising to 25 kws @ summer solace.  Have recently had installed a solar diverter to a storage hot water system, thereby sending excess solar to heat hot water prior to exporting to the grid.  Entire system equates to no electricity bill for approx. 6 months per year (excess electricity exported to the grid also covers supply charges for same period).  Bills for balance of the year are < $100/quarter.  Installing the solar system & diverter are proving highly cost effective with payoff projected by 5th year.Note I also have a pre-exisitng (previous house owner installed) 1 kw system of west roof installed by Pyramid Power, which is good for offsetting late spring through to mid autumn afternoon electricity usage, but this system delivers negligble electricity in winter.",
